      "writtenOn": "2022-07-29T04:22:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "pm_debug_messages is much too coarse; it enables a large amount of log output during every suspend/resume cycle of which at most 1 line is helpful for investigating this recurring class of battery life issues.  Deploying builds with pm_debug_messages is therefore not viable, as it substantially shortens the temporal span of the log.  The new vendor hook will only emit logs specific to this class of problem, and only when the problem actually manifests.\n\ntl;dr - the new hook is a scalpel alternative to the pm_debug_messages chainsaw.",
      "parentUuid": "91af0e5a_454fcaf6",
      "revId": "d5bc54642cc1f9b99c18e73e4402fc45b25d3e3d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
